speechtext:
Answers to Questions 1 and 2: Subsidies and support payments have been made to or for the benefit of producers during the years 1960-1968, in the following amounts: 19601961, $103,805,000;	1961-1962, $140,055,000;
1962-1963, $55,611,000; 1963-1964, $86,119,000; 1964-1965, $79,631,000; 1965-1966, $100,967,000; 1966-1967, $135,770,000; 1967-1968, $154,766,000; 1968-1969, $165,841,000.
The above figures include payments made by the Agricultural Stabilization Board, the Canadian Dairy Commission and the Canadian Livestock Feed Board, plus payments made under other Departmental Support programs for Crop Insurance, Hog and Lamb premiums, compensation and sundry emergency assistance.
